  "description": "DIGQAN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H54 Dy4 N32 O8 2+,2(C13 H14 N8 O1),2(Cl1 1-),20(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy5 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.754-3.762 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.17-114.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [(L3-2H)2(L3-H)2(L3)2Dy4(OH)4]Cl2(H2O)20. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 20 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
